completed_at: "2026-09-07T13:55:21.691Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 45
acceptance_criteria: Physical and aliased output roots retain original source mapping and sourcesContent; second compaction is byte-identical; runtime function names and declarations remain intact; macOS nightly validation passes.
goal: project management = context management
value: Stable packaged source attribution across supported platforms
why_now: New GitHub report exposes an uncovered boundary in required release or agent workflows.
parent: pm-u9d0
risk: low
confidence: high
resolution: Resolve the physical output root for both esbuild entrypoints and output mapping during runtime compaction.
expected_result: "Original source mapping, declarations, runtime names and repeated-compaction bytes remain stable through physical and aliased build roots."
actual_result: The real directory-alias regression failed before the fix and now passes alongside the physical-root fixture. Original sourcesContent and exact second-compaction bytes are preserved. Full exact coverage and static gates pass; hosted macOS verification remains required before merge.
